t of newly onset symptoms of anxiety and distress : a systematic review with network meta-analysis of randomized trials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-767433","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Digital methods, taken up in the collection and analysis of data, raise concerns around extraction, representation, care, consent, and participation familiar to feminist methodologies. At a feminist STS lab, specialising in digital methods, we convened some workshops to support research design in ongoing projects situated in the Lab’s community, with the aim to articulate feminist principles for digital methods. These projects, working with methods including digital ethnography, database implementation, and machine learning design raise feminist questions around centring care in data collection and participation, navigating hesitancies around extracting data from vulnerable subjects, and working through representational politics of data. These workshops, rather than congealing a set of feminist principles, generated a proliferation of disconcertments and troubles. We offer workshopping troubles as a way to navigate and theorise tensions in designing digital methods research. We account for how these workshops served as a method to elicit troubles, surfacing them for further analysis, and helped us shift from binding dichotomies to troubles that open ongoing inquiry. We reflect on how digital methods return us to troubles that, while well understood in feminist approaches to data, require articulation in practice and research design.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Perriam, Jessamy","Cohn, Marisa","Hockenhull, Michael","Tatjana Reime, Lara","Landa, Luis","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Friis, Henriette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730171"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Disconcertment","Ethnography","Feminist digital methods","Research Design","Science and Technology Studies","workshopping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"workshopping troubles towards feminist digital methods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08164649.2024.2321576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730171","identifier":[{"id":"85186618045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-63137823-9862-4f33-a0d3-440a4269c108"],"keyword":["Feminist digital methods","disconcertment","ethnography","research design","science and technology studies","workshopping"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-70A0FC14E3B5B57117B14FBB1F3E6C98"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08164649.2024.2321576","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampau","last":"Perriam","locid":"4ca57c3b-1d1f-4ecf-87b0-fe690510c887","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","orcid":"0000-0002-6362-8634","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"hockenhullpau","last":"Hockenhull","locid":"5041f387-908f-4845-9f79-3a6dbd527f4b","name":"Hockenhull, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2670-2102","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lara","key":"reimepau","last":"Reime","locid":"0baaf9f8-3126-4cb1-b22f-b9fceabb8b54","name":"Tatjana Reime, Lara","name_org":"Reime, Lara","orcid":"0000-0002-7475-2147","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis","key":"landapau","last":"Landa","name":"Landa, Luis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"140f881b-1540-455b-8066-f0bc9ac6d82c","name":"Friis, Henriette","orcid":"0009-0008-1098-6674","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-63137823-9862-4f33-a0d3-440a4269c108"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Workshopping Troubles: Towards Feminist Digital Methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730171","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper advocates for the potential of feminist participatory practices to create conditions for inclusive and equitable futures. It addresses the need to design for transformative feminist futures and challenges normative innovation spaces. The authors reflect on their experiences organising two feminist hackathons, emphasising intersectionality, equity, and collaboration. They present 11 design principles that guided their efforts, highlighting the importance of centring local grassroots organisations. The paper discusses the potential of these design principles as tools for community engagement, nurturing collective imagination, and normalising feminist practices in collaborative spaces. It emphasises the importance of moving from embodied knowledge to embodying knowledge and integrating values and experiences into the infrastructure of innovation events. The authors acknowledge the challenges in operationalising principles, such as valuing labour and expertise, and raise questions about commitment and responsibility in inclusive, feminist events. This work contributes to the discourse on designing conditions for co-creating feminist imaginaries.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Friis, Henriette","Sánchez, Eva Duran","Marttila, Sanna-Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789574"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Feminist Futures Helsinki Initiative"],"keyword":["Co creation","Community engagement","Intersectionality","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design principles for co creating feminist imaginaries","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.1034","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789574","ids":["itu-d1cb1831-72bf-4d5a-8ba4-8b3114b45d42"],"keyword":["Co-creation","Community engagement","Feminist informatics","Intersectionality","Participatory design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1AC528D58C30FD845E0D204522EBF48A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.1034","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"feminist futures helsinki initiative","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Feminist Futures Helsinki Initiative","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"140f881b-1540-455b-8066-f0bc9ac6d82c","name":"Friis, Henriette","orcid":"0009-0008-1098-6674","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Duran","key":"sánchezpau","last":"Sánchez","name":"Sánchez, Eva Duran","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2024.1034","status":"p","title":"DRS2024: Research Papers"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d1cb1831-72bf-4d5a-8ba4-8b3114b45d42"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Design Principles For Co-creating Feminist Imaginaries","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789574","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Most soft tissue sarcoma (STS) patients do not respond to traditional checkpoint inhibitor treatment, which may be due to infiltrating immunosuppressive tumour-associated macrophages. This study investigated the prognostic value of four serum macrophage biomarkers. Methods: Blood samples were taken from 152 patients with STS at the time of diagnosis; clinical data were prospectively collected. The concentrations of four macrophage biomarkers (sCD163, sCD206, sSIRPα, sLILRB1) were measured in serum, dichotomised based on median concentration, and evaluated either individually or when combined with established prognostic markers. Results: All macrophage biomarkers were prognostic of overall survival (OS). However, only sCD163 and sSIRPα were prognostic for recurrent disease (sCD163: hazard ratio (HR): 1.97 (95% CI: 1.10–3.51) and sSIRPα: HR: 2.09 (95% CI: 1.16–3.77)). A prognostic profile was made based on sCD163 and sSIRPα; it also included c-reactive protein and tumour grade. Patients with intermediate- or high-risk prognostic profiles (adjusted for age and tumour size) had a higher risk of recurrent disease compared to low-risk patients (HR: 2.64 (95% CI: 0.97–7.19)) and (HR 4.3 (95% CI: 1.62–11.47)), respectively. Conclusion: This study demonstrated that serum biomarkers of immunosuppressive macrophages were prognostic for OS; when combined with well-established markers of recurrence they allowed for a clinically relevant categorising of patients.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aggerholm-Pedersen, Ninna","Friis, Henriette Nymark","Baad-Hansen, Thomas","Møller, Holger Jon","Sandfeld-Paulsen, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-247410"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Aggerholm-Pedersen, Ninna"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Immune system","Macrophage","Sarcoma","sCD163","sCD206"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"macrophage biomarkers scd000000000163 and ssirpα in serum predict mortality in sarcoma patients","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers15051544","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-247410","identifier":[{"id":"36900335","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10000605","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85149882678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ce9fb014-5311-42bb-9d70-8edfa1daf262"],"keyword":["biomarkers","immune system","macrophage","sCD163","sCD206","sLILRB1","sSIRPα","sarcoma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBFB74721E4C9EFEE0B6F773472CAD77"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers15051544","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/422068480/cancers-15-01544-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Experimental Clinical Oncology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oncology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ninna","key":"aggerholmpedersenpau","last":"Aggerholm-Pedersen","locid":"2647dec1-4e3f-4d05-a5c3-b86a20317d62","name":"Aggerholm-Pedersen, Ninna","orcid":"0000-0002-6859-5296","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henriette Nymark","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"e4528bf0-355f-4958-9d23-99d01d6d27d9","name":"Friis, Henriette Nymark","orcid":"0009-0001-5089-1687","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"baadhansenpau","last":"Baad-Hansen","locid":"73f367ed-4c3c-432c-95d9-73ab20b05f09","name":"Baad-Hansen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4826-8412","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger Jon","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"b08dc9ce-d595-49c6-833a-4ec9b4223a05","name":"Møller, Holger Jon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"sandfeldpaulsenpau","last":"Sandfeld-Paulsen","locid":"2140d46f-90c2-4419-a0ef-1e17b994bfee","name":"Sandfeld-Paulsen, Birgitte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36900335"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers15051544","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"5","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"1544","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149882678"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ce9fb014-5311-42bb-9d70-8edfa1daf262"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Macrophage Biomarkers sCD163 and sSIRPα in Serum Predict Mortality in Sarcoma Patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-247410","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Spontaneous pregnancy loss occurs in approximately 1 in 4 pregnancies; however, diagnostic workup is mostly restricted to women with recurrent pregnancy loss. The lack of workup on first pregnancy loss is likely a result of the high de novo fetal aneuploidy rate; however, this ignores the association of euploid pregnancy loss with an increased risk of future losses. Diagnosis of ploidy is advantageous but requires collection of pregnancy tissue. Cell-free fetal DNA (cffDNA) has revolutionized prenatal screening and has shown evidence in 2 small studies of diagnostic utility in pregnancy loss. The prospective Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss (COPL) study is a large initiative with the overall aim to explore the causes of pregnancy loss. This prospective cohort study of women from the COPL aimed to investigate the clinical utility of cffDNA-based testing in women with pregnancy loss. Adult women with a pregnancy loss before gestational age 22 weeks seen between November 2020 and May 2022 at 1 of the 3 participating COPL sites were invited to participate. Blood samples for cffDNA analysis were obtained before treatment to remove pregnancy tissue or within 24 hours of passage of pregnancy tissue. Pregnancy tissue was collected for direct sequencing and comparison to cffDNA results. Aneuploidy was assessed for all chromosomes, and discordant results were considered false-positive if the cffDNA result was aneuploid and false-negative if the cffDNA result was euploid. A total of 1000 women were recruited and underwent cffDNA blood draws, and 32% of women either did not manage to collect pregnancy tissue or collected a sample classified as unknown tissue. The cffDNA result was inconclusive in 112 (11%) of initial cases due to a low fetal fraction or low sequencing quality and were excluded from sensitivity and specificity analysis. The association between inconclusive results and gestational age was approximately 10% from gestational age 7 weeks on, whereas results were inconclusive approximately 50% of the time at earlier gestational ages. The final cohort for analysis thus included 888 cases, 446 (50%) of which were euploid, 405 (46%) aneuploid, and 37 (4%) contained multiple aneuploidies. The sensitivity of cffDNA testing compared with direct sequencing of pregnancy tissue was 85% (95% confidence interval [CI], 79–90), specificity was 93% (CI, 88–96), and accuracy was 89% (95% CI, 85–92). The results of this study demonstrate that cffDNA-based testing has a high sensitivity, specificity, and accuracy for the diagnosis of ploidy when compared with direct sequencing of pregnancy tissue. In addition, approximately a third of women were not able to collect true pregnancy tissue, illustrating the importance of introducing a pregnancy tissue-independent alternative for diagnostics in pregnancy loss.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","Ambye, Louise","Gruhn, Jennifer R.","Petersen, Jesper Friis","Wrønding, Tine","Amato, Letizia","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Ji, Boyang","Bro-Jørgensen, Maiken Hemme","Werge, Lene","Petersen, Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","Brinkmann, Clara","Petersen, Julie Birch","Dunø, Morten","Bache, Iben","Herrgård, Markus J.","Jørgensen, Finn Stener","Hoffmann, Eva R.","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695912"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["BioInnovation Institute"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cell free fetal dna for genetic evaluation in copenhagen pregnancy loss study copl a prospective cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-695912","identifier":[{"id":"85163829377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6d784b63-fedb-4c4a-bda3-748b17b691d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C42CB7D39CA0DAFB4598A6F5400CD037"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["BioInnovation Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tanja Schlaikjær","key":"hartwigtanjaschlaikjærpau","last":"Hartwig","name":"Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"ambyelouisepau","last":"Ambye","name":"Ambye, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jennifer R.","key":"gruhnjenniferrpau","last":"Gruhn","locid":"d1b8c69f-7bff-4210-b193-5391514106df","name":"Gruhn, Jennifer R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jesper Friis","key":"petersenjesperfriispau","last":"Petersen","locid":"41d7917c-a9f8-4765-9057-1fed4304173d","name":"Petersen, Jesper Friis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tine","key":"wrøndingtinepau","last":"Wrønding","name":"Wrønding, Ti