","key":"nielsenhenriettesvarrepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0dbb49-ded3-4607-aca2-08fd68b6a558","name":"Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ogx.0000000000001163","issn":["00297828","15339866"],"issn_org":["00297828"],"issue":"6","journal":"Obstetrical and Gynecological Survey","pages":"345-346","status":"p","title":"Obstetrical and Gynecological Survey","volume":"78"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163829377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6d784b63-fedb-4c4a-bda3-748b17b691d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cell-Free Fetal DNA for Genetic Evaluation in Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss Study (COPL) : A Prospective Cohort Study","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695912","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":9,"contributors":["Boje, Amalie Dyhrberg","Egerup, Pia","Westergaard, David","Bertelsen, Marie-Louise Mathilde Friis","Nyegaard, Mette","Hartwell, Dorthe","Lidegaard, Øjvind","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre"],"cuid":["S02-090.87-685768"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reply of the authors endometriosis and pregnancy loss the importance of mitigating sources of bias","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fertnstert.2023.05.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.87-685768","identifier":[{"id":"85162860573","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37169324","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-d04e28ca-fd20-461a-af30-62d17abf8bd1","ku-33e36879-9633-41e8-bc36-f43a44e5a177"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E81FABCA6567827575D51923E5D91C1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fertnstert.2023.05.003","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Brunak Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Genomic Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Neuroboost"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie Dyhrberg","key":"bojepau","last":"Boje","name":"Boje, Amalie Dyhrberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia","key":"egeruppau","last":"Egerup","name":"Egerup, Pia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"David","key":"westergaardpau","last":"Westergaard","locid":"049e0f46-367a-4436-9553-149dfa1b62ac","name":"Westergaard, David","orcid":"0000-0003-0128-8432","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie-Louise Mathilde Friis","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","name":"Bertelsen, Marie-Louise Mathilde Friis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise","key":"mathildefriisbertelsenpau","last":"Mathilde Friis Bertelsen","name":"Mathilde Friis Bertelsen, Marie Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardpau","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"c048a688-cd64-40ca-a277-53f16360f7a1","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-4973-8543","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dorthe","key":"hartwellpau","last":"Hartwell","name":"Hartwell, Dorthe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Øjvind","key":"lidegaardpau","last":"Lidegaard","locid":"477519a8-a5d9-4dcf-970a-e11c7e4f936f","name":"Lidegaard, Øjvind","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henriette Svarre","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0dbb49-ded3-4607-aca2-08fd68b6a558","name":"Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37169324"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fertnstert.2023.05.003","issn":["00150282","15462501"],"issn_org":["00150282"],"issue":"2","journal":"Fertility and Sterility","pages":"393-394","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fertility and Sterility","volume":"120"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162860573"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d04e28ca-fd20-461a-af30-62d17abf8bd1","ku-33e36879-9633-41e8-bc36-f43a44e5a177"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reply of the Authors : Endometriosis and pregnancy loss: the importance of mitigating sources of bias","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.87-685768","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: One in four pregnancies end in a pregnancy loss. Although the effect on couples is well documented, evidence-based treatments and prediction models are absent. Fetal aneuploidy is associated with a higher chance of a next successful pregnancy compared with euploid pregnancy loss in which underlying maternal conditions might be causal. Ploidy diagnostics are therefore advantageous but challenging as they require collection of the pregnancy tissue. Cell-free fetal DNA (cffDNA) from maternal blood has the potential for evaluation of fetal ploidy status, but no large-scale validation of the method has been done. METHODS: In this prospective cohort study, women with a pregnancy loss were recruited as a part of the Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss (COPL) study from three gynaecological clinics at public hospitals in Denmark. Women were eligible for inclusion if older than 18 years with a pregnancy loss before gestational age 22 weeks (ie, 154 days) and with an intrauterine pregnancy confirmed by ultrasound (including anembryonic sac), and women with pregnancies of unknown location or molar pregnancies were excluded. Maternal blood was collected while pregnancy tissue was still in situ or within 24 h after pregnancy tissue had passed and was analysed by genome-wide sequencing of cffDNA. Direct sequencing of the pregnancy tissue was done as reference. FINDINGS: We included 1000 consecutive women, at the time of a pregnancy loss diagnosis, between Nov 12, 2020, and May 1, 2022. Results from the first 333 women with a pregnancy loss (recruited between Nov 12, 2020, and Aug 14, 2021) were used to evaluate the validity of cffDNA-based testing. Results from the other 667 women were included to evaluate cffDNA performance and result distribution in a larger cohort of 1000 women in total. Gestational age of fetus ranged from 35-149 days (mean of 70·5 days [SD 16·5], or 10 weeks plus 1 day). The cffDNA-based test had a sensitivity for aneuploidy detection of 85% (95% CI 79-90) and a specificity of 93% (95% CI 88-96) compared with direct sequencing of the pregnancy tissue. Among 1000 cffDNA-based test results, 446 (45%) were euploid, 405 (41%) aneuploid, 37 (4%) had multiple aneuploidies, and 112 (11%) were inconclusive. 105 (32%) of 333 women either did not manage to collect the pregnancy tissue or collected a sample classified as unknown tissue giving a high risk of being maternal. INTERPRETATION: This validation of cffDNA-based testing in pregnancy loss shows the potential and feasibility of the method to distinguish euploid and aneuploid pregnancy loss for improved clinical management and benefit of future reproductive medicine and women's health research. FUNDING: Ole Kirks Foundation, BioInnovation Institute Foundation, and the Novo Nordisk Foundation.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Schlaikjær Hartwig, Tanja","Ambye, Louise","Gruhn, Jennifer R.","Petersen, Jesper Friis","Wrønding, Tine","Amato, Letizia","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Ji, Boyang","Bro-Jørgensen, Maiken Hemme","Werge, Lene","Petersen, Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","Brinkmann, Clara","Petersen, Julie Birch","Dunø, Morten","Bache, Iben","Herrgård, Markus J.","Jørgensen, Finn Stener","Hoffmann, Eva R.","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","Freiesleben, Nina la Cour","Bliddal, Sofie","Søndergaard, Therese Juhlin","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Sørensen, Erik","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Herregård, Markus J.","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Kolte, Astrid Marie","Westergaard, David","þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Stefánsson, Kári","Jónsson, Hákon","Magnússon, Ólafur","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Schmidt, Lone","Kristiansen, Karsten","Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","Nyegaard, Mette","Krog, Maria Christine","Løkkegaard, Ellen","Bredkjær, Helle Ejdrup","Wilken-Jensen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-094.13-005502"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["COPL consortium"],"level":"sci","mr