me":"Mathilde Friis Bertelsen, Marie-Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise Mathilde Friis","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","name":"Bertelsen, Marie Louise Mathilde Friis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardpau","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"c048a688-cd64-40ca-a277-53f16360f7a1","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-4973-8543","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dorthe","key":"hartwellpau","last":"Hartwell","name":"Hartwell, Dorthe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Øjvind","key":"lidegaardpau","last":"Lidegaard","locid":"477519a8-a5d9-4dcf-970a-e11c7e4f936f","name":"Lidegaard, Øjvind","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henriette Svarre","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8c0dbb49-ded3-4607-aca2-08fd68b6a558","name":"Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36608920"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fertnstert.2022.12.042","issn":["00150282","15462501"],"issn_org":["00150282"],"issue":"5","journal":"Fertility and Sterility","pages":"826-835","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fertility and Sterility","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150856105"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9b9e2869-a5ca-486c-81ee-db8aaf3c4f2d","ku-05fdb469-d799-4b9b-9398-7909e64bdcce"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Endometriosis is associated with pregnancy loss : A nationwide historical cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.55-672403","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Cold-water corals (CWCs) are important ecosystem engineers in the deep sea that provide habitat for numerous species and can form large coral mounds. These mounds influence surrounding currents and induce distinct hydrodynamic features, such as internal waves and episodic downwelling events that accelerate transport of organic matter towards the mounds, supplying the corals with food. To date, research on organic matter distribution at coral mounds has focussed either on seasonal timescales or has provided single point snapshots. Data on food distribution at the timescale of a diurnal tidal cycle is currently limited. Here, we integrate physical, biogeochemical, and biological data throughout the water column and along a transect on the south-eastern slope of Rockall Bank, Northeast Atlantic Ocean. This transect consisted of 24-h sampling stations at four locations: Bank, Upper slope, Lower slope, and the Oreo coral mound. We investigated how the organic matter distribution in the water column along the transect is affected by tidal activity. Repeated CTD casts indicated that the water column above Oreo mound was more dynamic than above other stations in multiple ways. First, the bottom water showed high variability in physical parameters and nutrient concentrations, possibly due to the interaction of the tide with the mound topography. Second, in the surface water a diurnal tidal wave replenished nutrients in the photic zone, supporting new primary production. Third, above the coral mound an internal wave (200 m amplitude) was recorded at 400 m depth after the turning of the barotropic tide. After this wave passed, high quality organic matter was recorded in bottom waters on the mound coinciding with shallow water physical characteristics such as high oxygen concentration and high temperature. Trophic markers in the benthic community suggest feeding on a variety of food sources, including phytodetritus and zooplankton. We suggest that there are three transport mechanisms that supply food to the CWC ecosystem. First, small phytodetritus particles are transported downwards to the seafloor by advection from internal waves, supplying high quality organic matter to the CWC reef community. Second, the shoaling of deeper nutrient-rich water into the surface water layer above the coral mound could stimulate diatom growth, which form fast-sinking aggregates. Third, evidence from lipid analysis indicates that zooplankton faecal pellets also enhance supply of organic matter to the reef communities. This study is the first to report organic matter quality and composition over a tidal cycle at a coral mound and provides evidence that fresh high-quality organic matter is transported towards a coral reef during a tidal cycle.","author_count":16,"contributors":["de Froe, Evert","Maier, Sandra R.","Horn, Henriette G.","Wolff, George A.","Blackbird, Sabena","Mohn, Christian","Schultz, Mads","van der Kaaden, Anna Selma","Cheng, Chiu H.","Wubben, Evi","van Haastregt, Britt","Møller, Eva Friis","Lavaleye, Marc","Soetaert, Karline","Reichart, Gert Jan","van Oevelen, Dick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-134453"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["de Froe, Evert"],"country":["Greenland","Netherlands","Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Nord University","Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","University of Agder","University of Liverpool","Utrecht University","Wageningen University & Research"],"keyword":["Benthic pelagic coupling","Cold water corals","Internal waves","Particulate organic matter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrography and food distribution during a tidal cycle above a cold water coral mound","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dsr.2022.103854","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-134453","identifier":[{"id":"85138044153","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-090631e8-6c49-4e60-a898-c314ca242d59"],"keyword":["Benthic-pelagic coupling","Cold-water corals","Diurnal tidal cycle","Internal waves","Organic matter transport","Particulate organic matter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11D1F0CEF842B2355A1C411F38085A51"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/332847466/1_s2.0_S0967063722001662_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dsr.2022.103854","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands institute for sea research nioz","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of agder","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Agder","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Applied Marine Ecology and Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"nord university","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nord University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"nl","key":"wageningen university research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Wageningen University & Research","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Evert","key":"defroepau","last":"de Froe","name":"de Froe, Evert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra R.","key":"maierpau","last":"Maier","name":"Maier, Sandra R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette G.","key":"hornpau","last":"Horn","name":"Horn, Henriette G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"George A.","key":"wolffpau","last":"Wolff","name":"Wolff, George A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabena","key":"blackbirdpau","last":"Blackbird","name":"Blackbird, Sabena","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"mohnpau","last":"Mohn","locid":"3249f637-7852-40ab-b6ac-1b8670bcd9c9","name":"Mohn, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-4331-1365","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","name":"Schultz, Mads","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Selma","key":"vanderkaadenpau","last":"van der Kaaden","name":"van der Kaaden, Anna Selma","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiu H.","key":"chengpau","last":"Cheng","name":"Cheng, Chiu H.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Evi","key":"wubbenpau","last":"Wubben","name":"Wubben, Evi","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Britt","key":"vanhaastregtpau","last":"van Haastregt","name":"van Haastregt, Britt","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva Friis","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"b6bcca6a-bc33-4771-b944-4a952088440e","name":"Møller, Eva Friis","name_org":"Moller, Eva Friis","orcid":"0000-0002-7640-3514","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"lavaleyepau","last":"Lavaleye","name":"Lavaleye, Marc","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karline","key":"soetaertpau","last":"Soetaert","name":"Soetaert, Karline","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Gert Jan","key":"reichartpau","last":"Reichart","name":"Reichart, Gert Jan","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dick","key":"vanoevelenpau","last":"van Oevelen","name":"van Oevelen, Dick","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.dsr.2022.103854","issn":["09670637","18790119"],"issn_org":["09670637"],"journal":"Deep-Sea Research Part I: Oceanographic Research Papers","paperid":"103854","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Deep-Sea Research Part I: Oceanographic Research Papers","volume":"189"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138044153"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-090631e8-6c49-4e60-a898-c314ca242d59"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hydrography and food distribution during a tidal cycle above a cold-water coral mound","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-134453","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Based on epidemiological and animal studies, the rationale for using polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFAs) as a treatment for Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) seems promising. Here, the objective was to systematically identify and critically assess the evidence from clinical trials. The primary outcome was ADHD core symptoms. The secondary outcomes were behavioral difficulties, quality of life, and side effects. We performed a systematic search in Medline, Embase, Cinahl, PsycInfo, and the Cochrane Library up to June 2020. The overall certainty of evidence was evaluated using Grades of Recommendation, Assessment, Development, and Evaluation (GRADE). We identified 31 relevant randomized controlled trials including 1755 patients. The results showed no effect on ADHD core symptoms rated by parents (k = 23; SMD: −0.17; 95% CI: −0.32, −0.02) or teachers (k = 10; SMD: −0.06; 95% CI: −0.31, 0.19). There was no effect on behavioral difficulties, rated by parents (k = 7; SMD: −0.02; 95% CI: −0.17, 0.14) or teachers (k = 5; SMD: −0.04; 95% CI: −0.35, 0.26). There was no effect on quality of life (SMD: 0.01; 95% CI: −0.29, 0.31). PUFA did not increase the occurrence of side effects. For now, there seems to be no benefit of PUFA in ADHD treatment; however, the certainty of evidence is questionable, and thus no conclusive guidance can be made. The protocol is registered in PROSPERO ID: CRD42020158453.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Händel, Mina Nicole","Rohde, Jeanett Friis","Rimestad, Marie Louise","Bandak, Elisabeth","Birkefoss, Kirsten","Tendal, Britta","Lemcke, Sanne","Callesen, Henriette Edemann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-220961"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Händel, Mina Nicole"],"keyword":["ADHD","Adolescents","Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder","Children","Fatty acids","Meta analysis","Omega 3","Systematic review"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Health Authority"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy and safety of polyunsaturated fatty acids supplementation in the treatment of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder adhd in children and adolescents a systematic review and meta analysis of clinical trials","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu13041226","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-220961","identifier":[{"id":"85103832625","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8068201","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33917727","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a0d0ac59-d0c2-43a5-9026-8e2a12ebd749"],"keyword":["ADHD","Adolescents","Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder","Children","Fatty acids","Meta-analysis","Omega 3","Polyunsaturated","Systematic review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6CBCDD72F5B8CA8ED548F06B3A0A8E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu13041226","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Health Authority"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mina Nicole","key":"händelpau","last":"Händel","name":"Händel, Mina Nicole","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanett Friis","key":"rohdepau","last":"Rohde","name":"Rohde, Jeanett Friis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise","key":"rimestadpau","last":"Rimestad","locid":"9acd38f0-aea4-41d2-ad63-419ee15ea5fc","name":"Rimestad, Marie Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-2115-1620","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth","key":"bandakpau","last":"Bandak","name":"Bandak, Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"birkefosspau","last":"Birkefoss","name":"Birkefoss, Kirsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Britta","key":"tendalpau","last":"Tendal","name":"Tendal, Britta","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sanne","key":"lemckepau","last":"Lemcke","locid":"78d93747-da82-4b87-933b-facc596fbd06","name":"Lemcke, Sanne","orcid":"0000-0002-0542-713X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette Edemann","key":"callesenpau","last":"Callesen","name":"Callesen, Henriette Edemann","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33917727"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu13041226","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"4","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"1226","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103832625"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a0d0ac59-d0c2-43a5-9026-8e2a12ebd749"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Efficacy and safety of polyunsaturated fatty acids supplementation in the treatment of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (Adhd) in children and adolescents : A systematic review and meta-analysis of clinical trials","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-220961","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: In the last decade, there has been an increased interest in exploring the impact of the physical birth environment on midwifery practice and women's birth experiences. This study is based on the hypothesis that the environment for birth needs greater attention to improve some of the existing challenges in modern obstetric practice, for example the increasing use of augmentation and number of interventions during delivery. STUDY DESIGN: A randomized controlled trial was carried out to study the effect of giving birth in a specially designed \"birth environment room\" on the use of augmentation during labor. The study took place at the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Herning Hospital, Denmark and included 680 nulliparous women in spontaneous labor at term with a fetus in cephalic presentation. Women were randomly allocated to either the \"birth environment room\" or a standard birth room. The primary outcome was augmentation of labor by use of oxytocin. Secondary outcomes were duration of labor, use of pharmacological pain relief, and mode of birth. Differences were estimated as relative risks (RR) and presented with 95% confidence intervals. RESULTS: No difference was found on the primary outcome, augmentation of labor (29.1% in the \"birth environment room\" versus 30.6% in the standard room, RR 0.97; 0.89-1.08). More women in the \"birth environment room\" used the bathtub (60.6% versus 52.4%, RR 1.18; 1.02-1.37), whereas a tendency to lower use of epidural analgesia (22.6% versus 28.2%) did not reach statistical significance (RR 0.87; 0.74-1.02). The chance of an uncomplicated birth was almost similar in the two groups (70.6% in the \"birth environment room\" versus 72.6% in the standard room, RR 0.97; 0.88-1.07) as were duration of labor (mean 7.9 hours in both groups). CONCLUSIONS: Birthing in a specially designed physical birth environment did not lower use of oxytocin for augmentation of labor. Neither did it have any effect on duration of labor, use of pharmacological pain relief, and chance of birthing without complications. We recommend that future trials are conducted in birth units with greater improvement potentials.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lorentzen, Iben Prentow","Andersen, Charlotte S","Jensen, Henriette Svenstrup","Fogsgaard, Ann","Foureur, Maralyn","Lauszus, Finn Friis","Nohr, Ellen Aagaard"],"cuid":["S02-094.27-021188"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lorentzen, Iben Prentow","Lorenzen, Iben Prentow"],"country":["Australia","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Newcastle","University of South-Eastern Norway"],"keyword":["Birth environment","Birth experience","Birth outcome","Birth room design","Birth unit design","Oxytocin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does giving birth in a birth environment room versus a standard birth room lower augmentation of labor results from a randomized controlled trial","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eurox.2021.100125","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.27-021188","identifier":[{"id":"85102565555","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33817626","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8010388","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-748b006e-4a57-4d6d-bee4-0da4466a173c","sdu-6adde8d1-29e4-43e8-872e-ce0a7accafbd"],"keyword":["Birth environment","Birth experience","Birth outcome","Birth room design","Birth unit design","Oxytocin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3BE16EA45CF8D720B24A8FDFC01313CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eurox.2021.100125","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/181619802/1_s2.0_S2590161321000053_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Kvindesygdomme og Fødsler, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Herning"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of newcastle","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Newcastle","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"no","key":"university of south eastern norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of South-Eastern Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben Prentow","key":"lorentzenpau","last":"Lorentzen","locid":"faa0f4c3-ea77-466d-bc4e-46853e4b949d","name":"Lorentzen, Iben Prentow","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben Prentow","key":"lorenzenpau","last":"Lorenzen","name":"Lorenzen, Iben Prentow","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte S","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Charlotte S","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette Svenstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Henriette Svenstrup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":"fogsgaardpau","last":"Fogsgaard","name":"Fogsgaard, Ann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maralyn","key":"foureurpau","last":"Foureur","name":"Foureur, Maralyn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn Friis","key":"lauszuspau","last":"Lauszus","locid":"81bc2970-7c93-4775-a544-7f1c158a42e1","name":"Lauszus, Finn Friis","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen Aagaard","key":"nøhrpau","last":"Nøhr","locid":"7cacab04-e162-47a1-8d07-cf73fa62b4fc","name":"Nohr, Ellen A","name_org":"Nøhr, Ellen Aagaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7039-1105","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33817626"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eurox.2021.100125","issn":["25901613"],"journal":"European Journal of Obstetrics and Gynecology and Reproductive Biology: X","paperid":"100125","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Obstetrics and Gynecology and Reproductive Biology: X","title_org":"European Journal of Obstetrics & Gynecology and Reproductive Biology: X","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102565555"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-AL