ity of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab1eb48d-4349-4a0b-93a6-337836a725e0","sdu-634062ab-2e56-4248-a383-d472d1743d9b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Dense sampling of bird diversity increases power of comparative genomics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.91-045217","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aims/hypothesis: Adopting a diet containing indigestible fibre compounds such as prebiotics to fuel advantageous bacteria has proven beneficial for alleviating inflammation. The effect of the microbial changes on autoimmunity, however, remains unknown. We studied the effects of prebiotic xylooligosaccharides (XOS) on pancreatic islet and salivary gland inflammation in NOD mice and tested whether these were mediated by the gut microbiota. Methods: Mother and offspring mice were fed an XOS-supplemented diet until diabetes onset or weaning and were compared with a control-fed group. Diabetes incidence was monitored, insulitis and sialadenitis were scored in histological sections from adult mice, and several metabolic and immune variables were analysed in mice before the development of diabetes. Gut barrier function was assessed using an in vivo FITC-dextran permeability test. The importance of XOS-mediated gut microbial changes were evaluated in antibiotic-treated mice fed either XOS or control diet or given a faecal microbiota transplant from test animals. Results: Diabetes onset was delayed in the XOS-fed mice, which also had fewer cellular infiltrations in their pancreatic islets and salivary glands. Interestingly, insulitis was most reduced in the XOS-fed groups when the mice were also treated with an antibiotic cocktail. There was no difference in sialadenitis between the dietary groups treated with antibiotics; the mice were protected by microbiota depletion regardless of diet. Faecal microbiota transplantation was not able to transfer protection. No major differences in glucose–insulin regulation, glucagon-like peptide-1, or short-chain fatty acid production were related to the XOS diet. The XOS diet did, however, reduce gut permeability markers in the small and large intestine. This was accompanied by a more anti-inflammatory environment locally and systemically, dominated by a shift from M1 to M2 macrophages, a higher abundance of activated regulatory T cells, and lower levels of induction of natural killer T cells and cytotoxic T cells. Conclusions/interpretation: Prebiotic XOS have microbiota-dependent effects on salivary gland inflammation and microbiota-independent effects on pancreatic islet pathology that are accompanied by an improved gut barrier that seems able to heighten control of intestinal diabetogenic antigens that have the potential to penetrate the mucosa to activate autoreactive immune responses.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hansen, Camilla H.F.","Larsen, Christian S.","Petersson, Henriette O.","Zachariassen, Line F.","Vegge, Andreas","Lauridsen, Charlotte","Kot, Witold","Krych, Łukasz","Nielsen, Dennis S.","Hansen, Axel K."],"cuid":["S02-099.95-023011"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Camilla H.F."],"keyword":["Gut barrier","Gut microbiota","Insulitis","Mucosal immunology","Prebiotics","Sialadenitis","XOS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeting gut microbiota and barrier function with prebiotics to alleviate autoimmune manifestations in nod mice","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-019-4910-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.95-023011","identifier":[{"id":"31139852","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85066480992","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000478770300017","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-8df5e86c-63ac-497d-9900-89e812ace4db","ku-e102d820-f4d2-45c7-88e3-e8d5d0a81b07"],"keyword":["Gut barrier","Gut microbiota","Insulitis","Mucosal immunology","Prebiotics","Sialadenitis","XOS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-12BFE42294B20B6D3220CA02C4F4046C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-019-4910-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla H. F.","key":"hansencamillahartmannfriispau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d7f25dbd-3efc-483b-9805-8909e9597652","name":"Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","name_org":"Hansen, Camilla H. F.","orcid":"0000-0002-1860-385X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian S.","key":"larsenchristianschiøthpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"48a39b03-cb85-4871-ad38-cb43987be59c","name":"Larsen, Christian Schiøth","name_org":"Larsen, Christian S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Henriette O.","key":"peterssonhenrietteopau","last":"Petersson","locid":"e1e735ec-6168-4711-9b51-ddc0cb0d8278","name":"Petersson, Henriette O.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line F.","key":"zachariassenlinefpau","last":"Zachariassen","locid":"cdafe75d-cfc9-4fca-adfe-20ae0c542b57","name":"Zachariassen, Line F.","orcid":"0000-0001-5425-9841","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"veggeandreaspau","last":"Vegge","name":"Vegge, Andreas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"lauridsencharlottepau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"892b1da6-ebd2-456b-b88e-0d709e529b1c","name":"Lauridsen, Charlotte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Witold","key":"kotwitoldpau","last":"Kot","locid":"1ed8825e-1c59-4e9b-bcd7-974d5f6d8f01","name":"Kot, Witold","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lukasz","key":"krychlukaszpau","last":"Krych","locid":"a9463259-048d-4fd6-8218-dde9fb94c96b","name":"Krych, Lukasz","orcid":"0000-0003-3224-1346","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis S.","key":"nielsendennissandrispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","name_org":"Nielsen, Dennis S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel K.","key":"hansenaxelkorneruppau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ecc439ea-5c9b-4e25-814a-3ee8960bc0d0","name":"Hansen, Axel Kornerup","name_org":"Hansen, Axel K.","orcid":"0000-0003-1575-2507","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31139852"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-019-4910-5","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"1689-1700","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066480992"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8df5e86c-63ac-497d-9900-89e812ace4db","ku-e102d820-f4d2-45c7-88e3-e8d5d0a81b07"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Targeting gut microbiota and barrier function with prebiotics to alleviate autoimmune manifestations in NOD mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-023011","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: In the last decade, there has been an increased interest in exploring the impact of the physical birth environment on birth outcomes. The birth environment might have an important role in facilitating the production of the hormone oxytocin that causes contractions during labour. Oxytocin is released in a safe, secure and confidence-inducing environment, and environments focused on technology and medical interventions to achieve birth may disrupt the production of oxytocin and slow down the progress of labour. An experimental “birth environment room” was designed, inspired by knowledge from evidence-based healthcare design, which advocates bringing nature into the room to reduce stress. The purpose is to examine whether the ‘birth environment room’, with its design and decor to minimise stress, has an impact on birth outcomes and the birth experience of the woman and her partner. Materials and methods: A randomised controlled trial will recruit 680 nulliparous women at term who will be randomly allocated to either the “birth environment room” or a standard room. The study will take place at the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at Herning Hospital, with recruitment from May 2015. Randomisation to either the “birth environment room” or standard room takes place just before admission to a birth room during labour. The primary outcome is augmentation of labour, and the study has 80% power to detect a 10% difference between the two groups (two-sided α = 0.05). Secondary outcomes are duration of labour, use of pharmacological pain relief, mode of birth, and rating of the birth experience by women and their partners. Trial registration: NCT02478385(10/08/2016).","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lorentzen, Iben","Andersen, Charlotte Sander","Jensen, Henriette Svenstrup","Fogsgaard, Ann","Foureur, Maralyn","Lauszus, Finn Friis","Nohr, Ellen A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821194"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lorentzen, Iben"],"country":["Australia","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of South-Eastern Norway","University of Technology Sydney"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study protocol for a randomised trial evaluating the effect of a birth environment room versus a standard labour room on birth outcomes and the birth experience","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.conctc.2019.100336","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was reported to the local scientific ethical committee and in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki. The study was granted exemption from requiring ethical approval by the Ethical committee (Reference number: 247/2014). The study has been reported to the Danish Data Protection Agency (reference number: 1-16-02-34-15) and the clinical trials registration website of the National Institutes of Health (NCT02478385). Board Name: The Central Denmark Region Committees on Health Research Ethics Board Affiliation: The Central Denmark Region Committees on Health Research Ethics. Phone: +45 7841 0182. Email: komite@rm.dk ."],"id":"S01-000.00-821194","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6402376","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6402376","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85062148298","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30886935","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-442461bb-a64d-4e97-b531-9423abfed4b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC6B9EF5E13D4F6B49BDE24CA6DDD76C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146727524/Study_protocol_for_a_randomised_trial_evaluating_the_effect_of_a_birth_environment_room_versus_a_standard_labour_room_on_birth_outcomes_and_the_birth_experience.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.conctc.2019.100336","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Herning"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of technology sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Technology Sydney","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"university of south eastern norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of South-Eastern Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben","key":"lorentzenpau","last":"Lorentzen","name":"Lorentzen, Iben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sander","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Charlotte Sander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette Svenstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"